ParseWasmModuleDoc
    Version: 1
    Language: en
    Format: STF
    Purpose: SIR port of the WASM parser: parses raw module bytes (runtime.wasm) into the rt structure used by GenWasm (types, imports, helper types, function/helper bodies, names).
    Provides: ParseWasm(data) -> rt. data is a WASM byte list; returns the rt section map (types, impmod, impname, helper_types, bodies, …).
    DependsOn: ReadLEB (LEB128 reading), Slice (section-body extraction).
    Composition: Native include from modules/GenWasm/GenWasm.sir (Path: ../ParseWasm/ParseWasm.sir).
    Notes: replaces the external runtime substitution — GenWasm parses the runtime itself via Sys.Input rtsrc, per the "SIR must cover all abstraction levels" requirement.
